        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: o arguido",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "o arguido — \"the accused, the formal suspect; the defendant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "O arguido não disse nada ao juiz. The accused said nothing to the judge."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A European legal term for someone formally named as a suspect in a criminal case, through to the trial; in Brazil o réu or o acusado. Feminine a arguida."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arguido is the participle of arguir \"to accuse, to argue\" (EtymDB), from Latin arguere \"to make clear, to prove, to accuse\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
